From dca8ba72dbc09aef39fcaf47a57cd26c7b364c3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOW2AI <ivan.meer1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 19:16:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] fix(test): add missing jsdom dependency to unbreak
 vitest in ci
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the red "Quality & Build" on main (all day 2026-07-05): vitest
aborted with `MISSING DEPENDENCY  Cannot find dependency 'jsdom'` and every one
of the 39 forks workers failed to start (`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`), so "no tests"
ran and the unit-test job failed.

vitest.config.ts sets `environment: "jsdom"`, which requires the standalone
`jsdom` package as a direct dependency. It was never in package.json — it came
in transitively via `jest-environment-jsdom`, removed during the Jest->Vitest
migration. Local runs still passed because jsdom lingered in node_modules from
earlier installs, masking the gap; a fresh `npm ci` in CI does not install it.
This is why trackers claimed "292/292 passing" while CI was red.

Added jsdom@^26.1.0 to devDependencies and regenerated package-lock.json with a
clean npm userconfig so all-platform optional bindings (rolldown win32/linux)
are preserved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
